<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <%
        const comparisonLegacyExportsEnabled = (Array.isArray(exportFormats) ? exportFormats : [])
            .some((format) => String(format?.value || '').trim().toLowerCase() !== 'ltd');
        const pageTitle = 'Mii Website Comparisons - InfiniMii';
        const pageDesc = 'Draft comparison of Mii websites, archives, QR code libraries, Tomodachi sharing tools, official references, and Mii creation resources.';
        const canonicalUrl = `${baseUrl}/guides/comparisons`;
        const keywords = 'mii websites, mii website comparison, mii qr code websites, mii library, mii archive, tomodachi mii sharing';
        const breadcrumbs = [
            { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
            { name: 'Mii Website Comparisons', url: '/guides/comparisons' }
        ];
        const schemaType = 'TechArticle';
        %>
        <%- include('metaTags', { title: pageTitle, description: pageDesc, canonicalUrl, keywords }) %>
        <%- include('structuredData') %>
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="/global.css">
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="/utilityPages.css">
    </head>
    <body>
        <%- include('globalStyle') %>
        <%- include('header') %>
        <%- include('accountDisplay') %>
        <main class="content faq-content" role="main">
            <%- include('sidebar') %>
            <article class="faq-article">
                <h1>Mii Website Comparisons</h1>
                <p class="faq-lede">A working comparison of Mii archives, sharing sites, and utilities.</p>

                <nav class="faq-nav" aria-label="Mii Website Comparison Sections">
                    <h2>Browse This Comparison</h2>
                    <ul class="faq-nav-list">
                        <li><a href="#overview">Overview</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#comparison-table">Draft Website List</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#comparison-points">Comparison Points</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#notes">Notes to Fill In</a></li>
                    </ul>
                </nav>

                <section id="overview" class="faq-section">
                    <h2>Overview</h2>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <p>This draft lists the main jobs each service handles and the gaps noted when the page was last updated.</p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <section id="website-list" class="faq-section">
                    <h2>Website List</h2>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <h2><a href="/">InfiniMii</a></h2>
                        <p>
                            InfiniMii processes and renders Mii data on the site without a manual review queue. Uploads can stay private for backup or transfer between devices, or be published for others to browse.
                            It also includes Wii Remote transfer tools, a height and weight converter, and a browser-based Tomodachi Life child generator.
                            The archive includes official Nintendo Miis.
                            <%= comparisonLegacyExportsEnabled
                                ? "InfiniMii provides the download formats listed by its export tools, along with recreation instructions."
                                : "InfiniMii keeps original LTD files unchanged. Miis from earlier systems retain the compatible conversion options listed on the site." %>
                            InfiniMii accepts native Tomodachi Life: Living the Dream files. It creates previews when the LTD data has been verified against the recovered renderer. It does not approximate files that use unverified data. Some clothing, wardrobe, Canvas, user-generated content, and other app-specific data cannot yet be displayed.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <h2><a href="https://tomodachishare.com/">TomodachiShare</a></h2>
                        <p>
                            TomodachiShare focuses on sharing Miis, particularly those made for Tomodachi Life: Living the Dream.
                            This page previously described only its 3DS QR and manual-recreation workflows. InfiniMii can now render compatible LTD Miis, but does not create previews for files that use unverified data. This does not mean either service supports every clothing, wardrobe, Canvas, user-generated content, or app-specific item.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <h2><a href="https://www.miicharacters.com/">MiiCharacters</a></h2>
                        <p>
                            MiiCharacters was an early Mii-sharing site and still hosts many Miis, but appears inactive. The last visible upload dates to 2017, and newer submissions remain in an unreviewed verification queue.
                            Existing entries include 3DS and Wii U QR codes plus recreation instructions for Wii, 3DS, Wii U, and the discontinued Miitomo app. Its Wii instruction form also accepts an <code>.rcd</code> file after the extension is changed to <code>.mii</code>.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <h2><a href="https://www.miilibrary.com/">Mii Library</a> and <a href="https://new.miilibrary.com/">New Mii Library</a></h2>
                        <p>
                            Mii Library aims to document Miis used in an official capacity. It remains in development, and some pages contain dead links or placeholders.
                            Its records can include several download formats, renders, source and filename details, and notes about individual Miis.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <h2><a href="https://tomodachiplaza.app/">TomodachiPlaza</a></h2>
                        <p>
                            TomodachiPlaza also focuses on sharing Miis and launched after TomodachiShare. Unlike TomodachiShare, it does not process uploaded Mii data. Users instead record facial features and settings in a form, then provide screenshots or photos for the listing.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <h2><a href="https://miiwiki.org/">MiiWiki</a></h2>
                        <p>
                            MiiWiki is a dedicated Mii wiki. It is newer than the other archives listed here, and some articles remain short or unfinished. Useful reference pages include its <a href="https://miiwiki.org/wiki/List_of_games_with_Miis">list of games with Miis</a> and <a href="https://miiwiki.org/wiki/List_of_official_Miis/QR_codes">official Mii QR list</a>.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <h2><a href="https://tomodachimiis.com/">TomodachiMiis</a></h2>
                        <p>
                           TomodachiMiis shares screenshots that visitors can use to recreate Miis manually. It does not appear to process or render Mii data, or to record recreation settings in the way TomodachiPlaza does.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <h2><a href="https://miipedia.com/">Miipedia</a></h2>
                        <p>
                           Miipedia has mainly focused on Miitopia for Switch and now also accepts Tomodachi Life: Living the Dream listings. Miitopia entries provide an in-game access code.
                           Living the Dream entries record Mii features in a form. Their images are screenshots or photos uploaded by users.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </section>
                <section>
                    <h2>This page may be out of date</h2>
                    <p>
                        These services change, and this comparison may not reflect their latest features.<br><br>

                        If a listing is wrong or incomplete, <a href="/contact">contact us</a> so it can be corrected.
                    </p>
                </section>
            </article>
            <%- include('featuredMiis') %>
        </main>
        <%- include('footer') %>
    </body>
</html>
